% Goal
Implement the `pdd prompt` CLI command group and its `lint` subcommand.

% Role & Scope
You are an expert Python engineer implementing the `pdd prompt` command group. This module connects the `PromptLinter` engine to the Click-based CLI and handles user input and output formatting.

% Requirements
1. Define `prompt_group` (click.Group) and `lint` subcommand.
2. Positional argument: `path` (the prompt file or directory to lint). Support options: `--ambiguity` (flag), `--stories` (directory path), `--json` (flag), `--llm` (flag), `--apply` (flag).
3. Orchestration: Parse inputs, discover target files, invoke `PromptLinter`, and handle output formatting.
4. Use `rich` for colorful and structured terminal output.

% Dependencies
<pdd.core.prompt_linter><include>context/core/prompt_linter_example.py</include></pdd.core.prompt_linter>
<click><include>context/click_example.py</include></click>

% Deliverables
- Code: `pdd/commands/prompt.py`